Sometimes one wants to avoid the "automake/autoconf" machinery
and just use the available "./configure".
A problem with the Git timestamps has the effect to (try to) rerun
the automake machinery when performing the "Make" (and after the
./configure step).

A way out is to set a correct time ordering with:

touch aclocal.m4; sleep 1; touch Makefile.in; sleep 1; touch configure; sleep 1; touch config.h.in
